claimed: okay-script-multipart -- the first okay-script-site follow-on (filed 2026-09-06): multipart/form-data. Site.webOf currently parses only application/x-www-form-urlencoded into Web.form; an upload's Body.Bytes arrives verbatim and nothing reads it. Adds okay.script.api.Part(name, filename, contentType, bytes) and Web.parts / Web.file(name); non-file multipart fields land in Web.form too, so a page reads form("title") the same way for either encoding. A byte-level parser (okay.script.Multipart: boundary from the Content-Type, CRLF framing, Content-Disposition name/filename, binary-safe) -- no dependency. Tests through Site.handle with a binary file part; touches Api.scala, Site.scala, specs/okay-script.md, the example store.
